// AeroCLStrat — Slipstream deltas only.
// Every other branch behaves as in UniCLStrat (shared IUniCLStrat; range management in
// AeroCLRangeLib, position layer in AeroCLPositionLib) and is specified in UniCLStrat.tree.
// Tests: test/unit/AeroCLStrat.t.sol (mocks: test/mocks/AeroCLStratMocks.sol),
//        test/fork/AeroCLStratFork.t.sol (real WETH/USDT pool + CLFactory).

AeroCLStrat::constructor(DeploymentConfig _params)
├── Given factory in config is zero
│   └── It should revert with UniCLStratZeroAddress
├── Given the configured pool does not contain WETH
│   └── It should revert with UniCLStratInvalidPool
├── Given CLFactory.getPool(token0, token1, pool.tickSpacing()) returns address(0)
│   └── It should revert with UniCLStratInvalidPool
├── Given CLFactory.getPool(token0, token1, pool.tickSpacing()) returns a different pool
│   └── It should revert with UniCLStratInvalidPool
├── Given the pool is registered under a different tick spacing than pool.tickSpacing()
│   └── It should revert with UniCLStratInvalidPool
├── Given twapInterval is greater than MAX_TWAP_INTERVAL
│   └── It should revert with UniCLStratInvalidConfig
├── Given pool.observe cannot serve twapInterval
│   └── It should revert with UniCLStratPoolTWAPNotAvailable
├── Given the 6-field slot0 in-use observationCardinality is below max(ceil(interval / MAX_BLOCK_SECONDS), MIN_OBSERVATION_CARDINALITY)
│   └── It should revert with UniCLStratInsufficientObservationCardinality
├── Given the 6-field slot0 in-use observationCardinality equals MIN_OBSERVATION_CARDINALITY
│   └── It should deploy
└── Given valid parameters
    ├── It should store the Slipstream factory as an ICLFactory
    ├── It should cache tickSpacing from the provenance lookup
    ├── It should report name "Aero Concentrated Liquidity Strategy"
    └── It should report version "1.0.0" (independent of UniCLStrat 2.0.0)

UniCLStrat::constructor(DeploymentConfig _params)
└── Given the pool has the 6-field Slipstream slot0 layout
    └── It should revert (7-field decode fails), which is why AeroCLStrat exists

AeroCLPositionLib::slot0(IUniswapV3Pool _pool)
└── When reading spot state
    ├── It should decode the 6-field Slipstream slot0 through ICLPool
    └── It should be the only spot read (strategy gates, AeroCLRangeLib, mintPosition)

AeroCLStrat::setTwapInterval(uint32 _interval)
├── Given the 6-field slot0 in-use cardinality cannot cover the new window
│   └── It should revert with UniCLStratInsufficientObservationCardinality
└── Given the cardinality covers the new window
    └── It should update twapInterval

AeroCLStrat::setShortTwapInterval(uint32 _interval)
└── Given pool.observe cannot serve the new window
    └── It should revert with UniCLStratPoolTWAPNotAvailable

AeroCLStrat::deposit()
├── Given the pool is not calm (spot read via _slot0)
│   └── It should revert with UniCLStratNotCalm
└── Given the pool is calm
    └── It should mint liquidity into the Aero pool and pay it in uniswapV3MintCallback

AeroCLStrat::withdraw(address _receiver, uint256 _amount)
└── Given the pool is not calm
    └── It should still burn and send native ETH to the receiver

AeroCLStrat::rebalance()
├── Given the strategy is healthy
│   └── It should revert with StrategyIsHealthy
└── Given spot drifted outside rebalanceTickThreshold
    └── It should re-center the main range around the current tick

AeroCLStrat::sync()
├── Given the unstaked position accrued swap fees
│   └── It should poke them into tokensOwed and pendingPerformanceFeeInETH
└── Given CLFactory.getUnstakedFee(pool) is non-zero
    ├── It should accrue tokensOwed net of the unstaked-fee share
    └── It should report pendingPerformanceFeeInETH on the net amount

AeroCLStrat::emergencyExit()
└── Given the strategy is paused
    └── It should sweep held WETH (as ETH) and paired token to StrategyManager

DeployAeroCLStrat::run()
├── Given CLFactory.isPool(pool) is false or getPool(tickSpacing) does not match
│   └── It should fail before broadcast
├── Given pool.observe cannot serve TWAP_INTERVAL or SHORT_TWAP_INTERVAL (e.g. a fresh pool)
│   └── It should fail before broadcast
├── Given the in-use observationCardinality is below the window requirement
│   └── It should fail before broadcast (observe alone passes by extrapolation)
├── Given the pool fee cap is at or above MAX_QUOTE_DEVIATION_BPS
│   ├── When STRICT_FEE_CAP is unset, false, or unparsable
│   │   └── It should log a warning and still deploy
│   └── When STRICT_FEE_CAP is true or 1
│       └── It should fail before broadcast
├── Given the pool fee cap is below MAX_QUOTE_DEVIATION_BPS
│   └── It should pass even when STRICT_FEE_CAP is true
├── Given the pool has no swap-fee hook
│   └── It should use the static fee() as the cap
└── Given every probe passes
    └── It should deploy and log unstakedFee
